From 78ba1fc6d3dd17881480ee9b51a34aa5ad671d78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Gomez <da.gomez@kernel.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:10:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Show the running step and its output in dagu start

On a terminal, dagu start showed only a spinner and a step count, so a
step's output reached the terminal only through a stdout: /dev/stdout
redirect, which scrolled through the spinner with no step named.

The region takes the output from the output tap rather than the log
files, so it shows each line as the step writes it. A sub-DAG run in
the same process reports to the region of the run that started it,
since that is where fstests-style DAGs do their work. A DAG whose steps
redirect to the terminal keeps the old display, which their output
would otherwise scroll through. Reading keys keeps the terminal's
signals so Ctrl-C still stops the run, and is skipped for a background
job, which SIGTTOU would stop.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Gomez <da.gomez@kernel.org>
---
